  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/AdrianLopez98/NeoForge/zipball/v1.0.27",
  "body": "**Neo Forge 1.0.27** — play Magic: The Gathering against AI (Commander, Standard, draft, Quest, Ascent and more). Free and offline, built on the Forge rules engine.\n\n### Downloads\n\n- **Android:** `neoforge-1.0.27.apk`\n- **Mac:** `NeoForge-macOS-arm64.dmg` (Apple Silicon) or `NeoForge-macOS-x64.dmg` (Intel)\n- **Linux:** `NeoForge-linux-x64.tar.gz` (most PCs and the Steam Deck) or `NeoForge-linux-arm64.tar.gz` — extract it and run `NeoForge/bin/NeoForge`\n- **Windows:** on itch.io → https://dokkodolabs.itch.io/neo-forge\n\n**Automatic Android updates with [Obtainium](https://github.com/ImranR98/Obtainium):** add `https://github.com/AdrianLopez98/NeoForge` as an app. Every new version gets its own release here with the APK.\n\n### What's new\n\n- **Spell effects:** when a spell or ability resolves, it flies from whoever cast it to its target and bursts in its color: fire, purple smoke, water, leaves, light or sparks. A creature that's hit waits for the blow before going to the graveyard, and cast permanents materialize on the battlefield.\n- **Combat hits like in Arena:** the creature that deals damage lunges at what it hits, the damage number pops up over creatures and players, and a player's portrait shakes when they take damage.\n- **Commander entrances:** when a commander enters the battlefield, yours or an opponent's, it gets a short cinematic moment. Some famous ones bring their own: Sephiroth's black wing and feathers, Cloud's Omnislash and Jin Sakai's wind of Tsushima.\n- Both can be turned off in Settings (\"Spell and combat effects\" and \"Commander entrances\").\n- **Tapping a permanent whose ability can't be used tells you why:** it's tapped, it just arrived, or the card's own condition isn't met.\n- **Quest:** \"Export missing cards\" from a deck, and the prize pack screen no longer shows number keys that did nothing.\n- **Android:**\n  - Quest duels in other worlds (or in a Quest with chosen sets) give rewards and count again on Android 8–13.\n  - Naming a card (Liar's Pendulum and the like) is fast, with search and pages.\n  - In portrait, crowded rows scroll sideways instead of overlapping (a setting).\n  - System bars no longer cover the menus on some tablets.\n  - Tapping the ×N of a stack of identical tokens attacks with all of them; the ×N stays visible in tight rows.\n  - Choosing a player still lets you switch to an opponent's board to check it.\n  - Deck editor filters scroll, Ascent relics show their text on the card, and picking a commander in portrait works again.\n- **Forge updated.**\n"
